# Line endings.
#
# Shell scripts MUST check out as LF, even on Windows. `api/entrypoint.sh` runs
# as a container CMD, and the api service bind-mounts `./api:/app` — so the file
# the container executes is the one in the Windows working tree, not the one
# baked into the image. With CRLF the shebang becomes `/bin/bash\r`, the kernel
# looks for a binary of that name, and the container dies with the memorably
# unhelpful `exec ./entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory`.
#
# Git already stores these as LF; it was `core.autocrlf` converting them on
# checkout. Without this file every Windows clone reintroduces the bug, so a
# second developer hits it on his first `docker compose up -d`.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else a container executes or parses as a script.
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers are the exception — cmd.exe wants CRLF.
*.bat           text eol=crlf
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
